","original_code":"746.2419(8)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-04-27","finding":"Requirements for Feeding Infants - Other Use of Handwashing Sink: The hand washing sink in the infant classroom was observed being used to clean pacifiers as well as prepare bottles.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026241465","violation_type_title":"Requirements for Feeding Infants - Other Use of Handwashing Sink (26 TAC §746.2419(8))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220421-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3317-6","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220421","date":"2022-04-21","original_code":"746.3317(6)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-04-27","finding":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Use Sanitary Holders: The infant classroom had cheese and crackers for snack and were not provided a plate or napkin for their food to rest on. The food was emptied from the pre packaging onto the bare table. The toddler classroom did have their snack on paper towels.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026482053","violation_type_title":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Use Sanitary Holders (26 TAC §746.3317(6))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220418","date":"2022-04-18","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":3,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905740032","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905740032","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-04-18","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220418-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3317-6","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220418","date":"2022-04-18","original_code":"746.3317(6)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-04-21","finding":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Use Sanitary Holders: The toddler classroom was having goldfish for snack and were not provided a plate or napkin for their food to rest on. The food was emptied from the pre packaging onto the bare table.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026268002","violation_type_title":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Use Sanitary Holders (26 TAC §746.3317(6))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220418-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2431-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220418","date":"2022-04-18","original_code":"746.2431(2)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-04-21","finding":"Infant Daily Report - Times and Amount of Food: Each infants daily sheets was incomplete and lacked any information about the amount of food or bottles consumed. The information was not added on several of the daily sheets prior to pick up by the parents.","topic":"food","source_record_id":"1026468754","violation_type_title":"Infant Daily Report - Times and Amount of Food (26 TAC §746.2431(2))","topic_label":"Food & nutrition"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220418-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3407","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220418","date":"2022-04-18","original_code":"746.3407","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Maintenance of Building, Grounds and Equipment: There were various areas of the operation that require maintenance, including but not limited to broken outlets covers with sharp edges, soap dispenser cover that is broken, toy kitchenette that has a broken piece near the sink with a sharp edge, and a pencil sharpener that is only partially secured to the wall with an exposed screw protruding at eye level and the cover to the pencil sharpener is not secured over the grinding mechanism of the pencil sharpener. All identified hazards were fixed at inspection.  The two outlet covers were repaired with clear tape so that the sharp edge is not exposed. The sharp edge on the play kitchenette was also covered with tape to prevent the sharp edge from being a risk. The pencil sharpener was removed from the wall. The soap dispenser cover was replaced.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026508997","violation_type_title":"Maintenance of Building, Grounds and Equipment (26 TAC §746.3407)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220301","date":"2022-03-01","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":1,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905740031","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905740031","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-03-01","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220301-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1401-d","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220301","date":"2022-03-01","original_code":"746.1401(d)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-03-29","finding":"Substitutes, Volunteers and Contractors - Counted in Ratio: The contracted caregiver counted in ratio received one hour of child abuse training in recognizing, reporting, and preventing abuse.     However annual training that is still lacking includes health and safety training in emergency preparedness; preventing and controlling the spread of communicable diseases, including immunizations; administering medication, if applicable, preventing and responding to emergencies due to food or an allergic reaction; understanding building and physical premises safety, including identification and protection from hazards that can cause bodily injury such as electrical hazards, bodies of water, and vehicular traffic; and handling, storing, and disposing of hazardous materials.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026510619","violation_type_title":"Substitutes, Volunteers and Contractors - Counted in Ratio (26 TAC §746.1401(d))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220208","date":"2022-02-08","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":1,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905740030","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905740030","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-02-08","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220208-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1401-d","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220208","date":"2022-02-08","original_code":"746.1401(d)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-03-01","finding":"Substitutes, Volunteers and Contractors - Counted in Ratio: One contracted caregiver that is counted in ratio does not have documentated annual training hours for her last complete training year of 7/22/2019 to 7/22/2021.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026522257","violation_type_title":"Substitutes, Volunteers and Contractors - Counted in Ratio (26 TAC §746.1401(d))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-94161-i20220131","date":"2022-01-31","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905897971","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905897971","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27